.TH BATTERY-NOTIFY 1 "2026-09-29" "simple-battery-notify" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
battery-notify \- battery notifications from UPower
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B battery-notify
.RB [ \-\-daemon ]
.br
.B battery-notify
.BR \-\-help " | " \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
Without options,
.B battery-notify
shows a notification with the current battery level and time remaining.
.PP
With
.BR \-\-daemon ,
it runs in the background, listens to UPower over D-Bus, and shows
notifications when the charger is connected or disconnected and when the
battery reaches the levels set in the configuration. It is meant to run as the
systemd user service
.BR battery-notify.service :
.PP
.RS
.nf
systemctl \-\-user enable \-\-now battery-notify.service
.fi
.RE
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-daemon
Run in the background.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage information.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/battery-notify/config.json
Your configuration. If absent,
.I /etc/battery-notify.json
is used.
.PP
The format is described in the README, installed at
.IR /usr/share/doc/simple-battery-notify/README.md .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR upower (1),
.BR notify-send (1)
.SH BUGS
Report issues at https://github.com/Davi-S/simple-battery-notify/issues
